# Netlify redirects. One file, three sites — evsuae.com, evsoman.com, evsqtr.com —
# so every destination below has to exist on ALL THREE. Verified 4 Sep 2026.
#
# THE ONE RULE: never point a redirect at a page that does not exist.
#
# Four rules in this file used to break it. They sent old URLs to
# /battery-replacement, /pre-purchase-inspection, /ac-repair-service and
# /brake-service — pages from the pre-Next site that were never rebuilt — so
# Google followed a 301 and landed on a 404. That is worse than no rule at all:
# a plain 404 is dropped, a redirect chain into one is crawled again and again.
# Search Console had 19 not-found and 23 page-with-redirect URLs, and 12 of the
# 14 chains tested ended dead.
#
# So: after editing this file, fetch every source URL once and confirm the chain
# ends at 200. There is a script for it in the scratchpad; the check takes a minute
# and is the whole reason this comment exists.

